{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0010: The visible test split is 4 volumes, byte-identical to train, verified by tree digest. Never select on it.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_competition_corpus.py | 6 passed", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "value": "The local test split is not a held-out evaluation set. It contains four volumes and no ground truth at all, and every one of the four is byte-identical to a train volume carrying the same dataset id, confirmed by matching tree digests over 456,757,564 to 547,662,847 bytes each. It is a format example for the submission pipeline; the genuinely held-out data is the hidden set swapped in at rerun."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0011: 199 datasets are 2 embryos, not 199 subjects: 6bba has 128 fields of view, 44b6 has 71.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_competition_corpus.py | 6 passed", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "value": "The supervised corpus spans two embryos, not 199 independent subjects. Dataset ids are {embryo}_{field_of_view}, and the 199 annotated train datasets divide into embryo 6bba with 128 fields of view and embryo 44b6 with 71."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0013: 133,318 annotated nodes / 128,883 edges against 4,725,117 estimated - 2.82% annotated, ranging 0.13-20.21% per dataset.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: artifacts/corpus-annotation-survey.json | 199 datasets surveyed, all carrying an estimate", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "value": "Annotation density varies by two orders of magnitude across the corpus and differs systematically between the two embryos. Across 199 annotated datasets there are 133,318 annotated nodes and 128,883 annotated edges against a summed estimated_number_of_nodes of 4,725,117, so 2.821 percent overall. Per dataset the annotated fraction ranges from 0.13 to 20.21 percent with a median of 3.56. Embryo 44b6 has a median density of 0.77 percent across 71 movies; embryo 6bba has 9.71 percent across 128."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0014: DIVISION SCARCITY: 151 annotated divisions in the whole corpus; 112 of 199 datasets have none. LOEO trains divisions on 26 (44b6) or 125 (6bba) examples.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: artifacts/corpus-annotation-survey.json | 151 divisions across 199 datasets", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "value": "Division supervision is extremely scarce. The corpus contains 151 annotated divisions in total, and 112 of the 199 datasets contain none at all. The median dataset has zero and the maximum has five. Embryo 44b6 holds 26 divisions and embryo 6bba holds 125, so a leave-one-embryo-out fold trains a division model on either 26 or 125 examples."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0021: NO intensity band can call any voxel background: the dimmest annotated cell sits at percentile 0.09. Audited over all 133,318 nodes, zero excluded.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate mask-audit | artifacts/mask-audit.json, 199 datasets, 133,318 nodes, 1699 seconds", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "value": "Audited over every annotated node in the corpus rather than a sample, no intensity band survives on either fold, the class prior is valid at every scale, and no annotated cell is lost to the model grid. All 133,318 annotated nodes across 18,933 annotated frames were measured, with zero excluded by sampling and zero falling outside the strided grid, so coverage is exact. The dimmest annotated cell sits at percentile 0.2987 on 44b6 and 0.0628 on 6bba, so band selection returns nothing for BOTH folds, not only 6bba: the q50 band that appeared to survive on 44b6 under four-frame sampling does not survive the full population. The q90 band would call 4,877 of 20,197 44b6 nodes (24.1 percent) and 16,336 of 113,121 6bba nodes (14.4 percent) background. Grid collisions are zero, so the count of positive voxels equals the annotated node count exactly. The class prior spans 1.443e-4 to 3.000e-3 per grid voxel with a median of 6.832e-4, every dataset inside the open unit interval. Annotated cells are local intensity maxima for 12.0 percent of 44b6 and 6.1 percent of 6bba."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0022: The SCAR assumption nnPU relies on is NOT supported: annotation density correlates with annotated-cell intensity at Pearson r=+0.354. Densely annotated movies carry BRIGHTER annotations.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate mask-audit | artifacts/mask-audit.json, selection_bias_probe, 199 datasets", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "value": "The SCAR assumption that nnPU relies on is not supported by this corpus. Across the 199 training datasets, annotation density correlates with the median intensity percentile of the annotated cells at Pearson r = +0.354. Labelling is therefore not independent of the feature the detector reads, and the direction is that densely annotated movies carry brighter annotations, not dimmer ones."}
