{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "threshold_lever_dead", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "6bba's threshold-limited miss class is 0.1% of GT (10 of 9,604)", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "data", "value": "The detection-threshold lever is DEAD on 6bba: only 0.1% of GT (10 of 9,604) is threshold-limited. Dropping tau from 0.96875 to 0.01 buys +0.10pp of GT reach for +167% nodes - catastrophic under the node-count multiplier."}
{"claim_type": "decision", "confidence": "high", "key": "d1_falsifier", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "**Kill unless `fork_at_matched_mother` rises from 0 to >= 25 across the 89 metric-reachable divisions**", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "value": "D1 kill condition, preregistered: replay both LOEO folds with the re-gated proposer and KILL unless fork_at_matched_mother rises from 0 to >=25 across the 89 metric-reachable divisions. If forks land at true mothers but divJ does not rise, the fault has moved to _is_strongly_connected_division (division_metrics.py:227-271)."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "fp_and_fn_are_disjoint", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The 613 FP forks and the 146 FN divisions are disjoint populations. Re-ranking, filtering, or re-scoring the forks we already emit recovers exactly ZERO divisions - the fork is never in the right place to begin with.", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "value": "DECISIVE: of the 146 FN divisions, ZERO have a fork emitted at the matched mother, in both folds. Re-ranking, filtering or re-scoring the forks we already emit recovers exactly ZERO divisions. Precision work cannot add a single TP."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "gate_widening_table", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "| 15.0 | 33 | **81** |  ... raising both to (15, 10) admits 81 of 89 - an 8x increase in what is even proposable.", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "value": "Widening both gates to (sister 15, parent 10) raises admissible divisions from 10 to 81 of the 89 metric-reachable - an 8x increase. Both gates must move: raising sister alone saturates at 33/89 because the parent gate then binds."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "high", "key": "honest_fitting_protocol", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Fit on 44b6's 26 divisions, evaluate on 6bba's 125, and separately the reverse; report both directions and take the min.", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "value": "With 26 divisions in 44b6 and 125 in 6bba, never fit on pooled events and report pooled. Fit on 44b6's 26, evaluate on 6bba's 125, then the reverse, report both directions and take the min."}
