{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0025: Multi-scale Difference-of-Gaussians dominates the classical local-max detector at a matched proposal budget (0.6154 vs 0.3846 reach).", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx.proposals.dog, measured against biohubx.proposals.classical | 26 annotated nodes, window estimated cells 56.7; classical 75 / 0.3846 and 310 / 0.7692; DoG 20 / 0.1923, 44 / 0.4231, 58 / 0.5000, 73 / 0.6154, 104 / 0.6538, 228 / 0.7308, 483 / 1.0000", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "A multi-scale Difference-of-Gaussians proposal source on the isotropic grid dominates the classical local-maximum detector on the recall-versus-budget frontier, on the F-0017 window. At a matched proposal budget the classical detector at threshold 0.70 emits 75 proposals and reaches 0.3846 annotated nodes within the official 7 micrometre radius, while DoG at response quantile 0.997 emits 73 and reaches 0.6154. At matched reachability the classical detector needs 310 proposals for 0.7692 while DoG needs 228 for 0.7308. DoG reaches 1.0000 at 483 proposals, which is 8.51 times the window's estimated cell count and carries a node-count multiplier of 0.2488."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0026: DoG reaches roughly TWICE the annotated cells of the classical detector, on both embryos, at every budget swept.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals | artifacts/proposals.json, 199 movies, 0 skipped, 491.9 seconds", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "A multi-scale Difference-of-Gaussians proposal source reaches roughly twice as many annotated cells as the classical local-maximum detector, on both embryos, at every node budget swept. Over all 199 annotated training movies at two annotated frames each, covering 394 annotated nodes on 44b6 and 1,762 on 6bba, reachability at the neutral budget of one times the estimated cell count is 0.7614 against 0.3528 on 44b6 and 0.6288 against 0.3610 on 6bba. Selecting the budget on one embryo and freezing it before measuring the other, both folds improve: fold_44b6 selects ratio 2.0 and reads 0.7770 against 0.4523 on held-out 6bba, and fold_6bba selects ratio 2.0 and reads 0.7944 against 0.3629 on held-out 44b6. At the one point where the two sources emit almost the same number of proposals, 6bba with classical at 31,045 and DoG at 31,482, DoG reaches 0.5539 against 0.4523."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0027: Reachability plateaus on 44b6 and still climbs on 6bba out to 8x the estimated cell count; one-to-one node recall tracks reach within 0.01.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --audit-misses | artifacts/proposals-e04b.json, 199 movies, 2,033 nodes audited, 654.6 seconds", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "Extending the DoG budget sweep to eight times the estimated cell count, the reachability curve plateaus on 44b6 and is still rising slowly on 6bba, and one-to-one node recall tracks reachability to within 0.01 everywhere. Over all 199 annotated training movies at two annotated frames each, DoG reaches 0.8046 at the neutral budget on 44b6 and 0.8807 from ratio 6 onward, where it emits about 87,000 proposals against an allowance of 336,000 and cannot fill the budget; on 6bba it reaches 0.6385 at the neutral budget, 0.9001 at ratio 6 and 0.9092 at ratio 8. The classical detector saturates at 0.3629 and 0.4546 from ratio 2 onward on the same movies. Selecting the budget on one embryo and measuring the other, fold_44b6 reads 0.9001 against 0.4546 and fold_6bba reads 0.8807 against 0.3629. Auditing the 2,033 annotated nodes at the neutral budget, the 69 missed on 44b6 and 617 missed on 6bba sit at median intensity percentile 0.919 and 0.955 within their frame against 0.988 and 0.994 for reached nodes, at median DoG response percentile 0.915 and 0.969 against 0.989 and 0.997, with no difference in annotated crowding or boundary distance, and with a proposal already lying within 14 micrometres of 87 percent of 44b6 misses and 50 percent of 6bba misses."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0028: Residual misses differ by embryo: on 44b6 it is a LOCALISATION failure, not a detection failure - a proposal already lies within 10um of 73% of missed cells.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --audit-misses --audit-ratio 8.0 | artifacts/proposals-residual-r8.json, 2,033 nodes audited, 450.9 seconds", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "The annotated cells DoG still misses at eight times the estimated cell count are two different populations on the two embryos. On 44b6 the residual is 44 of 365 nodes (12.1 percent) and is a localisation failure: the missed cells have median intensity percentile 0.897 within their frame with none below 0.50, median DoG response percentile 0.888, and a proposal already lies within 10 micrometres of 73 percent of them and within 14 of 93 percent, at a median nearest distance of 9.08 micrometres, just outside the official 7 micrometre radius. On 6bba the residual is 160 of 1,668 nodes (9.6 percent) and is half dimness: 60 percent sit below intensity percentile 0.80 and 10 percent below 0.50, median DoG response percentile 0.877, with a proposal within 10 micrometres of 44 percent and within 14 of 78 percent. On neither embryo do annotated crowding within 10 micrometres (4.5 and 1.3 percent) or proximity to a volume face (16 percent within 5 micrometres on both) distinguish the residual from reached cells."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0029: The near-miss residual is in-plane, not a z artefact: median in-plane offset 7.46/7.85um against median |z| 3.25/4.88.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --audit-misses, with the nearest-proposal displacement recorded | artifacts/proposals-residual-r8-displacement.json, 2,033 nodes audited, 613.5 seconds", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "The near-miss residual is not sub-voxel error and not a z artefact. Among the annotated cells DoG still misses at eight times the estimated cell count whose nearest proposal lies within 14 micrometres, 41 on 44b6 and 125 on 6bba, the displacement from cell to nearest proposal is dominated by the plane: median in-plane offset 7.46 and 7.85 micrometres against median absolute z offset 3.25 and 4.88, with z the larger component for only 29 and 22 percent. The signed z offset has no consistent direction, mean +0.83 and -1.05 micrometres, so there is no systematic depth bias. The in-plane offset's interquartile range, 5.8 to 8.9 on 44b6 and 6.4 to 9.8 on 6bba, is the spacing between neighbouring nuclei on a grid whose plane step is 1.625 micrometres."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0030: Greedy physical-radius suppression does NOT return local maxima - it packs the above-threshold region. Only 46 of 686 accepted points were strict 26-neighbourhood maxima.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx.proposals.dog against scipy.ndimage.maximum_filter, one frame | 686 accepted, 46 peaks, 6.7 percent; identical counts across three banks", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "Greedy physical-radius suppression does not return local maxima; it packs the above-threshold region, and on this data most of what it returns are shoulders of blobs. On frame 0 of 6bba_2540cd90 at the 0.95 response quantile, 13,108 of 262,144 strided voxels cleared the threshold, the suppression pass accepted 686 of them at a 4 micrometre radius, and only 46 of those 686 are strict 26-neighbourhood maxima of the response, against 37.8 estimated cells in the frame. Three different scale banks, (2.0, 3.0, 4.5), (2.0, 3.0) and (2.0, 2.5, 3.0), returned exactly 1,398 candidates on the same two-frame window, because the count is set by how much of the frame clears the quantile rather than by how many blobs there are."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0031: DoG BANK TUNING: dropping the 4.5um scale RAISES reachability on 44b6 everywhere; adding 2.5um changes nothing. Use (2.0, 3.0).", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --radii | artifacts/proposals-h11b-r23.json, artifacts/proposals-h11b-r2253.json", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "Removing the 4.5 micrometre scale from the DoG bank raises reachability on 44b6 at every budget and at every matched proposal count, and on 6bba only above twice the estimated cell count; adding a 2.5 micrometre scale changes nothing. Over all 199 annotated movies under the packed suppression regime of F-0027, the (2.0, 3.0) bank reaches 0.8782 against 0.8046 on 44b6 at the neutral budget, 0.9543 against 0.8680 at twice it, and plateaus at 0.9695 against 0.8807; at the baseline's own proposal counts it reads 0.9371 against 0.8680 and 0.9570 against 0.8756. On 6bba it reads 0.5936 against 0.6385 at the neutral budget, 0.7980 against 0.8093 at twice it, and at the baseline's count there 0.7796 against 0.8093, before overtaking at four times, 0.9115 against 0.8865, and eight, 0.9427 against 0.9092. The (2.0, 2.5, 3.0) bank matches (2.0, 3.0) to four decimals at every point. Selecting on one embryo and measuring the other, fold_44b6 reads 0.9115 and fold_6bba reads 0.9695 with the two-scale bank, against 0.9001 and 0.8807 with three scales."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0032: BEST MEASURED DETECTOR: strict 26-neighbourhood maxima on a (2.0,3.0)um DoG bank reaches 0.9239 (44b6) / 0.8984 (6bba) while emitting at or below the estimated cell count.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --local-maxima --radii 2.0,3.0 | artifacts/proposals-peaks-r23.json, artifacts/proposals-peaks-r2345.json", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "Requiring a DoG candidate to be a strict 26-neighbourhood maximum, with the two-scale bank (2.0, 3.0) micrometres, reaches 0.9239 of annotated cells on 44b6 and 0.8984 on 6bba while emitting at or below the estimated cell count, and does so with a third to a half of the proposals the packed detector needed to reach less. Over all 199 annotated training movies at two annotated frames each, the peaks detector saturates at 43,825 proposals on 44b6 against a neutral budget of 56,032, and at 50,159 on 6bba against 42,309; at the neutral budget it reads 0.9213 with 42,478 proposals on 44b6 and 0.7894 with 37,417 on 6bba, and at twice it 0.9239 and 0.8933. The packed detector with the three-scale bank, interpolated to the peaks detector's own proposal counts, reads 0.7159 on 44b6 and 0.6803 on 6bba. Under the peaks rule the large scale hurts on both embryos above the neutral budget: three scales saturate at 0.7665 and 0.8314 with 26,847 and 32,544 proposals, because neighbouring nuclei merge into one maximum at 4.5 micrometres; at the neutral budget on 6bba alone the three-scale bank still edges the two-scale one, 0.8048 against 0.7894. Selecting the budget on one embryo and measuring the other with the two-scale peaks detector, fold_44b6 reads 0.8933 on held-out 6bba at twice the estimate and fold_6bba reads 0.9239 on held-out 44b6 at four times it, against classical 0.4523 and 0.3629. The remaining misses at the neutral budget are 31 of 365 on 44b6, every one within 14 micrometres of a proposal and 84 percent within 10, and 368 of 1,668 on 6bba, of which 30 percent sit below intensity percentile 0.80 and 64 percent lie within 14 micrometres of a proposal."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0034: Per-scale strict peaks unioned before one shared suppression recovers what max-over-scales fusion loses; whether it helps depends entirely on the bank.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate proposals --per-scale-union | artifacts/proposals-h11c-union-r2345.json, artifacts/proposals-h11d-union-r23.json", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "method", "value": "Taking strict peaks at each DoG scale on its own and unioning them before one shared suppression pass (H-11c) recovers what the max-over-scales response loses to fusion, and whether that helps depends entirely on the bank. With the three-scale bank (2.0, 3.0, 4.5) the union saturates at 0.8376 reach on 44b6 with 37,596 proposals and 0.8842 on 6bba with 46,273, above the fused three-scale peaks (0.7665 and 0.8314) and below the frozen two-scale peaks (0.9239 and 0.8984), so the 4.5 micrometre scale costs more than fusion does. With the frozen two-scale bank (2.0, 3.0), H-11d, the union saturates at 0.9467 on 44b6 with 50,642 proposals and 0.9291 on 6bba with 60,587, above the frozen peaks by 0.023 and 0.031, and both held-out directions improve: fold_44b6 reads 0.9064 on held-out 6bba at twice the estimate against 0.8933, fold_6bba reads 0.9467 on held-out 44b6 at four times it against 0.9239. The gain is bought with proposals: the union emits 16 percent more on 44b6 and 21 percent more on 6bba at saturation, and at the neutral budget on the dense embryo it reads 0.7440 with 39,706 proposals against the frozen peaks' 0.7894 with 37,417, so its extra candidates outrank true cells there. On 44b6 at the neutral budget the two are level, 0.9188 against 0.9213."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0003: Unmatched predicted nodes are NOT edge false positives. Sets the whole economics of detection precision.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 11 passed", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "Under the pinned official scorer, a predicted node that matches no ground-truth node adds no edge false positive. Adding one isolated, unmatched node to a perfect two-node prediction left edge TP, FP, FN at 1, 0, 0 and the raw edge Jaccard at 1.0. An edge between two mutually unmatched predicted nodes is likewise uncharged. The exemption ends at the annotated cells: an edge whose source matches a ground-truth node that has a ground-truth successor, but which points elsewhere, was charged as one false positive."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0004: Node-count adjustment is clamped only at zero, so the multiplier exceeds 1 when under-predicting. Measured 1.09.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 11 passed", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "The official node-count adjustment multiplies the edge Jaccard by 1 - 0.1 * (N_pred - N_total) / N_total and is clamped only at zero, so the multiplier exceeds one whenever fewer nodes are predicted than the estimated total. With 2 predicted nodes, a declared estimated total of 20 and a raw edge Jaccard of 1.0, total_node_ratio was -0.9 and the adjusted edge Jaccard was 1.09."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0005: Frame-skipping edges are silently DROPPED by the scorer, not charged. Affects gap-recovery designs.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 11 passed", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "The two boundaries around a multi-frame edge behave differently and were measured separately. The Biohub-X lineage contract refuses an edge that does not advance exactly one frame at construction, so such an edge cannot reach evaluation. The pinned official scorer, called directly on a graph built beneath that contract, drops a frame-skipping edge instead of charging it: a prediction whose only edge ran from frame 0 to frame 2 produced edge TP 0, FP 0 and FN 2 against a ground truth of two consecutive edges."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0009: An edgeless graph is UNSCORABLE - evaluate() returns early and raises. A graph with no edges is a bug, not a low score.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/end_to_end/test_vertical_slice.py | 19 passed", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "A prediction that abstains on every target emits a graph with nodes and no edges, and the pinned official scorer cannot score it: `evaluate` returns early for an edgeless graph without applying its matching, so the `node_recall` helper it documents as requiring a matched graph raises a KeyError from inside tracksdata rather than returning a number. Biohub-X refuses such a prediction with a named error instead."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0015: Predicting the ANNOTATED count rather than the estimated total yields a median multiplier of 1.0964 (range 1.0798-1.0999).", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: artifacts/corpus-annotation-survey.json | 199 datasets, medians 1.0000 / 1.0929 / 1.0964 / 1.0982", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "The official node-count adjustment offers roughly a ten percent uplift on the raw edge Jaccard to a system that predicts the annotated node count rather than the true cell count. Using each dataset's own estimated_number_of_nodes, the multiplier 1 - 0.1 * (N_pred - N_total) / N_total has a median of 1.0000 when predicting the estimated total and 1.0964 when predicting the annotated count, ranging 1.0798 to 1.0999. It is 1.0992 for embryo 44b6 and 1.0903 for embryo 6bba."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0016: The division counter shares the unmatched-prediction exemption: an all-unmatched fork is uncharged but still raises num_pred_nodes.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: tests/contracts/test_official_scorer_behaviour.py | 13 passed", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "The official division counter shares the unmatched-prediction exemption that F-0003 measured for edges. A predicted fork built entirely from unmatched nodes is not charged: added to a perfect single-division prediction it left division TP, FP, FN at 1, 0, 0 and the division Jaccard at 1.0, while raising num_pred_nodes from 3 to 6 and lowering the adjusted edge Jaccard from 1.0 to 0.9. The exemption ends at the annotated cells: against a ground truth holding no divisions, a fork whose own node matched an annotated cell with a successor was charged as one division false positive, taking the division Jaccard from undefined to 0.0, and was charged again as one edge false positive."}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "medium", "key": "division_rarity", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The linking radius is 8.4 um, and divisions are one link in 853", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "~1 link in 853 is a division; a one-to-one linker scores 0.000 on divisions"}
{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "high", "key": "exploit_ceiling", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": null, "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "metric", "value": "Under-predicting nodes multiplies score by up to 1.10 (limit N_pred->0). Predicted nodes that match no GT node are NOT edge FPs, so every spurious detection is pure multiplier loss with zero jaccard gain."}
