{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0018: THE ECONOMICS OF THE NODE-COUNT LEVER: worth ~9% of adjusted edge Jaccard, and it stops paying once a filter destroys more than ~8% of correct edges.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate retention | artifacts/retention-oracle.json, 199 datasets, 1180 seconds", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "value": "Emitting the annotated node count instead of the estimated cell count is worth about nine percent of the adjusted edge Jaccard, and it stops paying once a filter destroys more than about eight percent of the correct edges to get there. Across all 199 annotated training datasets, a dense prediction padded to each dataset's own estimated_number_of_nodes scored an adjusted edge Jaccard of exactly 1.0000 on both embryo folds, because its node ratio is zero by construction. The same edges emitted at the annotated node count scored 1.0986 on 44b6 and 1.0905 on 6bba. Sweeping the fraction of correct edges the filtered policy retains, both folds break even at 0.92 and both fall behind the dense baseline at 0.90, by 0.0114 on 44b6 and 0.0184 on 6bba. Reaching 0.014 above the dense baseline, which is the step from a 0.936 system to 0.950 with the division term held fixed, requires a retention of 0.94 on both folds: 0.0327 on 44b6 and 0.0251 on 6bba."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0023: Minimum-track-length filtering with isolated-node pruning is near-free: 0.9963 / 0.9945 edge retention at span 6, with the division exemption.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate track-length | artifacts/track-length.json, 199 datasets, 133,318 nodes, 30.5 seconds", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "value": "A minimum-track-length filter with isolated-node pruning is nearly free in correct edges and nearly inert in node count when applied to the annotated graphs. Sweeping the minimum frame span over all 199 annotated training datasets, with the division exemption the public notebooks carry, edge retention at the span of 6 those notebooks use is 0.9963 on 44b6 and 0.9945 on 6bba, against the 0.94 target and 0.92 break-even F-0018 established. Every span from 2 to 10 clears both bars on both folds; even a span of 10 retains 0.9875 and 0.9763. Node retention tracks it closely, 0.9945 and 0.9928 at span 6, so the filter removes between 0.5 and 0.7 percent of annotated nodes. Dropping the division exemption changes retention by less than 0.002 anywhere in the sweep."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0033: ORACLE ASSOCIATION CEILING: with ground-truth-chosen edges over frozen strict peaks, 0.9961 on 44b6 but only 0.9227 on 6bba. Detection is still the binding constraint on 6bba.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate oracle-ceiling | artifacts/e06-oracle.json", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "value": "Over the frozen strict-peak proposals of D-0041, a legal graph whose edges are chosen with ground truth scores 0.9961 on 44b6 and 0.9227 on 6bba through the pinned official scorer, on ten-frame windows of all 199 annotated training movies. The 44b6 ceiling clears 0.950 and the 6bba ceiling does not, so under E06's preregistered rule association is not yet the sole bottleneck and the bake-off does not start. On 44b6, 1,811 of 1,970 annotated nodes matched a proposal one-to-one within 7 micrometres (0.9193), 1,544 of 1,750 annotated edges survived with both endpoints matched (0.8823), both retained divisions were kept, and 219,020 proposals stood against an estimated 280,156, a node ratio of -0.2182 that the official adjustment rewards: raw edge Jaccard 0.8823, adjusted 0.8961, division Jaccard 1.0. On 6bba, 9,208 of 10,157 nodes matched (0.9066), 7,852 of 8,949 edges survived (0.8774), 7 of 9 divisions were kept, and 275,566 proposals stood against an estimated 211,565, a node ratio of +0.3025 that the adjustment charges: raw edge Jaccard 0.8781, adjusted 0.8449, division Jaccard 0.7778. One 6bba window with 9 annotated edges retained no edge and could not be scored. The same detector configuration therefore under-proposes the sparse embryo by a fifth and over-proposes the dense one by a third; at a zero node ratio the 6bba ceiling would read 0.9559 and the 44b6 ceiling 0.9823, so the 6bba shortfall is proposal count before it is edge retention."}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "key": "F-0035: Truncating proposals to a budget chosen on the TRAINING embryo does not raise the held-out ceiling; the per-scale union without truncation does.", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "instrument: biohubx evaluate oracle-ceiling --budget-ratios, with and without --per-scale-union | artifacts/e05-peaks.json, artifacts/e05-union.json", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "value": "Truncating proposals to a budget chosen on the training embryo does not raise the oracle ceiling on the held-out embryo, and the per-scale union without truncation does. Over ten-frame windows of all 199 annotated movies, arm A0 (the frozen D-0041 peaks, untruncated) reproduces F-0033 exactly at 0.9961 on 44b6 and 0.9227 on 6bba, which is the check that the instrument change did not move the baseline. Budgeted selection is killed on its own falsifier: fold_44b6 selects k=1.5 on 44b6 (0.9962 against A0's 0.9961) and reads 0.9072 on held-out 6bba against A0's 0.9227, and the union arm A3 selects the same ratio and reads 0.9116, also below A0. Only the direction that selects on the dense embryo improves, and only trivially: fold_6bba picks k=2.0 and reads 0.9961 on held-out 44b6, equal to A0 to four decimals. Arm A2, the per-scale union with no truncation and therefore no constant to select, improves both directions at once: 1.0195 on 44b6 against 0.9961 and 0.9283 on 6bba against 0.9227. It buys that with proposals, 253,543 and 330,820 against 219,020 and 275,566, and pays the node-ratio charge on the dense embryo, +0.5637 against +0.3025, while raising its node match fraction from 0.9066 to 0.9300 and its edge retention from 0.8774 to 0.9107. No arm reaches 0.950 on 6bba; the best held-out reading on that embryo is A2's 0.9283."}
{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "medium", "key": "division_term_is_the_gap", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "score = adjusted_edge_jaccard + w * division_jaccard, with w = 0.1", "review_after": null, "status": "active", "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "value": "The 0.0235 gap between the 0.9465 public plateau and rank 1 (0.970) divided by the 0.1 division weight implies division_jaccard ~ 0.235 at rank 1. A competitor reported measuring 0.22 (topic 739516) and a one-to-one linker scores 0.000 (topic 733877). So the plateau is teams with working EDGES and ZERO divisions; the entire podium gap is the division term. This is an honest, defensible lever - no metric gaming required."}
